regress/gate_ab.sh:113:# GREEN.  The selftest below exercises run_emu_progress() with LITERAL arguments, so it proves
regress/gate_ab.sh:114:# the function works while proving nothing about the values this gate actually passes it --
regress/gate_ab.sh:115:# the rows guard a different instance of the thing they appear to guard.
regress/gate_ab.sh:116:#
regress/gate_ab.sh:117:# These bounds are derived, not taste: the observed maximum instructions-to-login is
regress/gate_ab.sh:118:# 7,785,570,754, so a budget below ~1.05x that would false-FAIL a healthy boot and one above
regress/gate_ab.sh:119:# ~2x stops bounding anything.  The stall threshold must exceed several -N record intervals
regress/gate_ab.sh:120:# (~3.4 s at the slowest rate measured) and stay far below the backstop.  The backstop must
regress/gate_ab.sh:121:# exceed the worst boot measured (742 s) with margin.  A static check costs no boot. ***
regress/gate_ab.sh:132:# #419 SELFTEST. The classifier decides whether a row is a regression, a hang, a harness fault
