regress/gate_ab.sh:134:# would cost 15 minutes and never be run. Fake "emulators" drive every reason in seconds.
regress/gate_ab.sh:135:#
regress/gate_ab.sh:136:# WHY THIS IS NOT OPTIONAL: the BUDGET and STALLED branches are ONLY EVER ENTERED BY A FAILING
regress/gate_ab.sh:137:# RUN, because a healthy boot stops at MARKER long before either. So nothing on a green run
regress/gate_ab.sh:138:# exercises them, and a mutation that breaks them is invisible to every capability row here.
regress/gate_ab.sh:139:#
regress/gate_ab.sh:140:# *** AND THE HARDEST CASE IS THE ONE THAT LOOKS HEALTHY. Remove `-N` and the guest still
regress/gate_ab.sh:141:# boots, still prints every marker, and still classifies as MARKER -- there is nothing wrong
