 611: 
 612:     #  wdcaltoffset PASS 1, 2026-08-30.  Four instruments from the measuring seat's
 613:     #  six-binary table.  CLASS_RESEARCH on the precedent two entries down: they are
 614:     #  EVIDENCE preserved so the numbers can be re-run rather than believed.
 615:     #
 616:     #  `table_a.py` is worth a note because it is the reason the table is credible:
 617:     #  it IMPORTS witness_20260829/wdcaltoff_rung3_probe.py rather than
 618:     #  re-implementing the encoder, so it cannot measure a fix of its own invention.
 619:     #  Its fix leg was checked byte-identical to mkfixleg.py's output AND to the
 620:     #  preserved fixleg.diff before any mutant was built.
 621:     #  #494 PASS 2, the opus5 seat.  Instruments preserved so its measured floor
 622:     #  breach can be re-run rather than believed.  `PROPOSED_...` is kept as the
 623:     #  PROVENANCE of what the seat proposed: the shipped detector differs from it
 624:     #  only by an added clause-(e) contract, and keeping both makes that checkable.
 625:     #  wdcaddtoinbufbound RUNG-3 WITNESS, 2026-08-30.  The probe is the INSTRUMENT of
 626:     #  a 20/20 two-leg measurement and is preserved so the numbers can be re-run
 627:     #  rather than believed.  `frozen_wave_*` is the FROZEN COPY the run actually
 628:     #  executed -- kept beside the live probe on purpose, because a comparison run
 629:     #  owes ONE instrument and the frozen copy is the proof of which one it was.
 630:     #  #497 widthkillclass, 2026-08-30.  The measuring seat's TWO-TABLE instrument set,
 631:     #  preserved so a 22-mutant result can be RE-RUN rather than believed.  CLASS_RESEARCH
 632:     #  on the precedent immediately below: these are EVIDENCE, not detectors the battery
 633:     #  owes a run.
 634:     #
 635:     #  `sgi_re_width_probe.py` is the 35-row detector ITSELF, and it is filed here as
