 781:     #  run -- same disposition as the repin2 frozen copy below.
 782:     #
 783:     #  It also carries a lesson worth keeping next to the code: its FIRST version anchored on
 784:     #  the handler's common tail, and `memory_writemax64(cpu, data, len, odata);' occurs FIVE
 785:     #  times across FOUR handlers in dev_sgi_re.c.  The anchor matched twice and the run
 786:     #  aborted.  This version anchors on SGIRE_W_UNMAP_* text and REFUSES unless the match
 787:     #  count is exactly 1, so a wrong-handler mutation is impossible rather than unlikely.
