 829:     #  sgireunmapped #499 KILL TABLE, 2026-08-31.  The table that discharged the three
 830:     #  undischarged accept rows (accept tlba/tlbb/tlbc) by MEASURED KILL -- M1/M2/M3 each
 831:     #  reddening exactly its own row -- and that found an L2 floor breach (M5) plus a
 832:     #  duplicate latch-bit defect #498 had silently introduced into the 08-30 generator.
 833:     #  CLASS_RESEARCH: evidence for a round, not detectors the battery owes a run.
 834:     #
 835:     #  *** `mkvariant499.py' REPLACES `opus_witness_20260830/mkvariant.py' AND THE REASON
 836:     #  MUST NOT BE PRUNED. ***  The older generator inserts `SGIRE_W_UNMAP_WR = 1 << 6',
 837:     #  and #498/cb28a6f added `SGIRE_W_DE_LEN = 1 << 6' to that same enum.  A duplicate
 838:     #  enumerator is legal C and silent, and DEVICE_ACCESS(sgi_de) casts the same struct,
 839:     #  so d->warned is SHARED -- measured as a 14/14 total escape.  This one uses 1<<7/1<<8
 840:     #  and hard-fails on duplicates.
 841:     #
 842:     #  `base_slot_probe.py' is the CONTROL for M5 and is what makes it a result rather than
 843:     #  a claim: it stores at the window BASE, reds on the mutant, and is serviced normally
 844:     #  on the fix.  Without it, `accept lina' staying green is merely a green row.
