 680:     #  #498's SHIPPING detector -- gate-wired in gate_arm.sh, 25 rows, sentinel
 681:     #  OPUS498T_DONE.  CLASS_DETECTOR rather than research: the battery owes it a run.
 682:     #  Self-contained by deliberate choice -- every committed probe in this tree rolls its
 683:     #  own pty rather than importing the untracked _scratchpad/gxprobe.py, and following
 684:     #  that precedent avoids making a committed file depend on one outside the repo.
 685:     "sgi_de_width_probe.py":
 686:         (CLASS_DETECTOR, "#498 sgidewidth -- 25 rows, gate_arm.sh, every row from a measured mutant kill"),
 687: 
 688:     #  sgireunmapped #499: the SHIPPED detector.  Gate-run by gate_arm.sh -- invocation,
 689:     #  OPUS499T_DONE sentinel check, controls by name, EVERY row named individually, and
 690:     #  a SUMMED denominator that separates a LOST row from a FAILING one.
 691:     #
 692:     #  *** THE ROW COUNT IS NOT WRITTEN HERE.  It went 28 -> 34 -> 36 -> 48 across four
 693:     #  passes in one day and this comment said 28 for all of them.  Derive it: ***
 694:     #
 695:     #      awk '/for v in "live"/{l=$0; getline n;
 696:     #           if (n ~ /UNMLOG/) {print gsub(/"[^"]*"/,"",l)}}' regress/gate_arm.sh
 697:     #
 698:     #  The `getline'/UNMLOG pair is load-bearing and is not defensive clutter: several
 699:     #  sections of gate_arm.sh open with the same `for v in "live" "devsig"' names, so
 700:     #  the FIRST match is a different probe's list.  The log variable on the NEXT line
 701:     #  is the only thing that identifies which section a row list belongs to.  (A first
 702:     #  attempt here counted `check "sgi_re unmapped row:"' lines and returned 1 -- the
 703:     #  rows are named in a LOOP, so there is one such line however many rows exist.
 704:     #  It was caught by running it, which is the whole reason a deriver is written down
 705:     #  instead of a number.)
 706:     #
 707:     #  (Demoted literals, kept as the record of what was measured and never as current
 708:     #  claims: 18/28 pre-fix and 28/28 on the fix, the test-first evidence in this row's
 709:     #  own artifacts dir; 30/34 and 33/34 for the two pass-2 mutants against the 34-row
 710:     #  repair, where the 28-row version had scored both 28/28.)
 711:     #  #500 sgideprimop: the SHIPPED detector.  Gate-run by gate_arm.sh -- invocation,
