```sh
# ---- #442: fbpending APPARATUS-ROT, no cap ------------------------------
# The bound's value is checked by the offline differential's R5 equality.
# Run synchronously after the A/B measurements have finished.
FBPENDING_STUB=$LOGDIR/fbpending_stub.bin
FBPENDING_LOG=$LOGDIR/fbpending_witness.log

if [ ! -x "$ROOT/build/gxemul" ]; then
    degrade "fbpending: HEAD binary missing or not executable"
elif ! command -v python3 >/dev/null 2>&1; then
    degrade "fbpending: python3 missing"
elif ! printf '\000\000\240\341' > "$FBPENDING_STUB" ||
     [ ! -r "$FBPENDING_STUB" ] ||
     [ "$(wc -c < "$FBPENDING_STUB")" != "4" ]; then
    degrade "fbpending: four-byte raw stub missing or could not be prepared"
else
    FBPENDING_RC=0
    python3 "$HERE/fbpending_witness.py" "$ROOT/build/gxemul" "$FBPENDING_STUB" > "$FBPENDING_LOG" 2>&1 || FBPENDING_RC=$?
    sed 's/^/       /' "$FBPENDING_LOG"

    check "fbpending: probe exit status" "$FBPENDING_RC" "0"
    check_min "fbpending: control rows actually reported" \
        "$(grep -cE '^  (ok|FAIL) ' "$FBPENDING_LOG")" 12
    check "fbpending: controls" \
        "$(grep -oE '^FBPENDING_CONTROL=[^[:space:]]+' "$FBPENDING_LOG")" \
        "FBPENDING_CONTROL=OK"
    check "fbpending: coverage" \
        "$(grep -oE '^FBPENDING_COVERAGE=[^[:space:]]+' "$FBPENDING_LOG")" \
        "FBPENDING_COVERAGE=OK"
    check "fbpending: symptom absent" \
        "$(grep -cFx 'FBPENDING_SYMPTOM=ABSENT' "$FBPENDING_LOG")" "1"
    check "fbpending: verdict" \
        "$(grep -cFx 'FBPENDING_VERDICT=PASS' "$FBPENDING_LOG")" "1"
fi
```

`"$ROOT/build/gxemul"` is the gate’s existing HEAD-binary expression; there is no existing `BIN` variable to reuse. Neither this gate nor the witness creates an existing four-byte fixture. The proposed gate section creates a little-endian ARM NOP; the witness subsequently plants its program through the debugger.

Coverage extraction deliberately permits the report’s explanatory suffix. An exact whole-line match against only `FBPENDING_COVERAGE=OK` would always fail.

Budget **120 seconds of requested free-run plus startup/debugger overhead**, approximately two minutes or more. These are source-derived costs, not measurements from this session.

[lib.sh](/C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/lib.sh:79) confirms that `check` compares strings and `check_min` compares integers. `degrade` continues execution and makes an otherwise successful gate SKIP at `gate_end`; recorded failures still take precedence. `gate_skip` exits immediately.

